efi/x86: add iMac18,3 to apple_match_product_name() for set_os

The iMac18,3's Apple firmware hides the Intel HD 630 (8086:5912) unless
something calls the set_os EFI protocol before the kernel starts. The
kernel already calls apple_set_os() for eight MacBook Pro models via
apple_match_product_name(). Adding iMac18,3 to that list makes the
firmware expose the Intel chip on this iMac too.

MacBookPro16,4 is replaced rather than appended: the array is declared
char[][15] and "MacBookPro16,4" is 14 bytes (15 with NUL), the same as
"iMac18,3" padded to 15. Replacing the last slot keeps the array size
and the EFI stub's .rodata layout identical.

Only safe alongside i915.disable_display=1 and a headless VBT. Without
them i915 invents an eDP connector on DDI A, which blanked the
Radeon-driven panel on iMac20,1.

Based on ahmadtv/omarchy-imac18-3 igpu/linux-side/mkinitcpio/imac-setos,
adapted as a compile-time source patch for NixOS.

--- a/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/x86-stub.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/x86-stub.c
@@ -307,7 +307,7 @@ static bool apple_match_product_name(void)
 		"MacBookPro14,3",
 		"MacBookPro15,1",
 		"MacBookPro15,3",
 		"MacBookPro16,1",
-		"MacBookPro16,4",
+		"iMac18,3",
 	};
 	const struct efi_smbios_type1_record *record;
 	const u8 *product;
